<article class="env-lemma" id="07A0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07A0">Lemma <span data-tag="07A0">21.13.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $K$ be a sheaf of sets on $\mathcal{C}$. Consider the morphism of topoi $j : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}/K) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$, see Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0791" data-tag="0791">7.30.3</a>. Then $j^{-1}$ preserves injectives and $H^ p(K, \mathcal{F}) = H^ p(\mathcal{C}/K, j^{-1}\mathcal{F})$ for any abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Sites, Lemmas <a href="/tag/04GZ" data-tag="04GZ">7.30.1</a> and <a href="/tag/0791" data-tag="0791">7.30.3</a> the morphism of topoi $j$ is equivalent to a localization. Hence this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/03F3" data-tag="03F3">21.7.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>